Package: openfuse-dkms
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: OpenFuse contributors <openfuse@invalid>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: dkms, patch, make
Recommends: curl | wget, mokutil, pkexec
Suggests: git, zstd
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Description: Arturia MiniFuse control support for snd-usb-audio (DKMS)
 OpenFuse adds the controls of the Arturia MiniFuse USB audio interfaces
 (INST and 48V switches, direct monitor mono, loopback mixer, level
 meters) to the ALSA snd-usb-audio driver as a mixer quirk.
 .
 This package rebuilds snd-usb-audio with DKMS for every installed kernel
 that has headers, from the sound/usb sources matching that kernel
 (downloaded, cached, or bundled in the package). Kernels for which no
 usable sources are found, or for which the module would not load under
 Secure Boot, are skipped and keep the distribution's snd-usb-audio.
 .
 Includes /usr/libexec/openfuse/openfuse-setup, a polkit-enabled helper
 for the OpenFuse installer (Secure Boot key enrollment, build, restore).
